A||||9||Bens88GT||Is Caster adjustable on Fieros?||||5||
Z||000000||Bens88GT||07-26-2000||10:32 AM||||Reason I ask is, I just took my 88GT to Midas for a 4-wheel alignment because it was pulling to the right, and after they did it, it still pulled to the right. Tire pressures are even, so it's not that.<P>The printout showed toe being perfectly balanced on each side, front and rear, and right in the middle of the specs. But camber was slightly more positive on the front left wheel than the front right, and caster was really crazy.<P>The front caster was 5.3 degrees on the left (in spec), but only 2.1 degrees on the right. That's pretty bad.<P>The guys at Midas told me yesterday that the camber and caster were not adjustable on my car, even though a different Midas shop had adjusted the camber during my last alignment. Today I went back and the guy said it's pulling to the right because of the camber difference, so they'd fix it.<P>But he said they can't adjust caster on my car, and I'm concerned about the right caster being so far off.<P>So... is the caster adjustable on Fieros?<P>Thanks,<BR>Ben||||reg||5
Z||000001||80's BOY||07-26-2000||11:08 AM||||yes, i am pretty sure caster is adjustable on a fiero. mine had the computer 4 wheel alignment after i put on the 16 incher's last year. it DOES require a kit though. sounds like the shop didn't want to fork over or simply did not have the info for it. the shop that did mine had a brand new machine and wanted to play with it so they kept my car a few days until the parts came in. i would ask your people about a caster kit and see what they say. how are the brakes? if you have one rubbing some, this could be the cause of you car pulling one way or the other. just a thought.<p>[This message has been edited by 80's BOY (edited 07-26-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000002||terryk||07-26-2000||12:14 PM||||Front only. The caster is adjusted with washers on the top control arm bolt. The washers are different thickness to allow the upper arm to be moved forwards or backwards and adjust caster.<P>The rear is locked in place and not a issue.<P>Yes, the shops want to be able to grab $40+ bucks to set the toe and tilt the struts. When they are faced with removing a bolt to adjust the caster, they go brain dead. I had to go an alignment shop. They did it quickly and didn't flinch. At one shop I have to explain to them how it worked, but they didn't have any shims/washers to adjust it.<P>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phoenix||07-26-2000||12:24 PM||||88's are different, they are adjustable without the use of shims or washers on the control arms.  I just had mine done at Tires Plus and they were able to do it just fine.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bens88GT||07-26-2000||12:55 PM||||Hey guys, thank you very much for the information! I'll go somewhere where they know what they're doing!<P>-Ben||||reg||10
Z||000005||terryk||07-26-2000||01:54 PM||||Sorry, I missed the 88 part. 84-87 only on the shims.||||reg||1
Z||000006||PJ||07-26-2000||09:39 PM||||There are two bolts that attach the rod the upper A-arm pivots on to the frame. They are adjustable in and out, fore and aft. The problem is you have to adjust for caster AND camber at the same time.  Try to change just the caster and nine times out of ten the camber moves also. Its virtually impossible to get perfect, but a 1/4 degree total tolerance is acceptable and not hard to get if you know what you're doing.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||07-27-2000||05:30 PM||||there is a ball joint replacement kit that has off center ball joints that can be turned after their mounted on A-arm to adjust caster and camber. I think there from Rayne Motorsports, if you need more infor email me and ill look them up for you. I think the whole kit is like $125, but there racing grade and youll never need to replace em again and adjusting them is a snap once there in.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||07-28-2000||02:52 AM||||The MOOG upper ball joints for the Fiero have slots for camber adjustment. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||PJ||07-28-2000||08:27 PM||||roger & Oreif:<P>I think Ben's got an '88 and you're referring to '84-'87 ball joints. I don't think they're interchangable. I just did a search for '88 uppers and they're no longer available from GM or anyone else as far as I know.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR>||||reg||1
